{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"1a1ac14852e5cb1c","name":"card_event_tank_wedge","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/Germany/OceaniaStorm/events/card_event_tank_wedge","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"TANK WEDGE","text":"Target friendly German tank and its adjacent units get +1+1.","flavorText":"The Panzerkeil, or “tank wedge,” was a German armoured tactic developed on the Eastern Front in response to increasingly dense Soviet anti-tank defenses. Tanks advanced in a wedge-shaped formation, with the heaviest and best-protected vehicles at the tip and lighter tanks spread along the flanks. At the Battle of Kursk in 1943, Tiger I tanks led the formations, with Panthers behind them and Panzer III and IV tanks forming the wings. This arrangement forced Soviet anti-tank gunners to constantly adjust their range as the formations advanced, while the heavier vehicles absorbed much of the incoming fire. The tactic met with mixed success. During Operation Citadel, elements of the 4th Panzer Army used the Panzerkeil to penetrate parts of the Soviet defensive system, while other German formations failed to break through and suffered heavy losses. Minefields posed a serious threat, often requiring combat engineers to advance ahead of the tanks and clear a path.","faction":"Germany","type":"order","rarity":"Uncommon","cost":1,"operationCost":0,"attack":0,"defense":0},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_event_tank_wedge","title":{"Namespace":"card_germany","Key":"card_event_tank_wedge_title","SourceString":"TANK WEDGE","LocalizedString":"TANK WEDGE"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::order","faction":"EFactionEnum::Germany","kredits":1,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_germany","Key":"card_event_tank_wedge_text","SourceString":"Target friendly German tank and its adjacent units get +1+1.","LocalizedString":"Target friendly German tank and its adjacent units get +1+1."},"flavorText":{"Namespace":"card_germany","Key":"card_event_tank_wedge_history","SourceString":"T